@module levels ; The level builder
@about BuildLevel $891A copies the level in Level from LevelData ($B000 + $87 x Level) to the grid LevelGrid $FD23 (15 cells a row and two guard bytes, 17 bytes a row; the row above and the guards are zero), clears the character map, marks every character to be drawn, and falls into RenderGrid and DrawMarkedChars: the level is in the buffers when it returns.
$8912 w LevelAddress 1 ; The current level's address in LevelData, and the renderer's and beam's character pointers
> LevelAddress: BuildLevel `$892A`, read by BuildLevel and SetUpLevel's count (`$8520`).
$8914 CharMapPointer ; the character map address being written: RenderGrid ($8963), and the beam's drawing ($90B9 on)
$8916 PixelPointer ; the beam's pixel-buffer address: $E7FF + 256 y + x ($90A7 on)
$8918 ; two bytes no code reads or writes
$891A c BuildLevel ; Copy level Level to the grid, clear the character map, mark every character; into RenderGrid
> 1. LevelAddress = LevelData `$B000` + `$87` x Level (by Level additions of `$87`).
> 2. LevelGrid `$FD00-$FDFA` cleared: the row above the grid (`$FD12`), the guards and whatever the mover left there.
> 3. The character map `$E000-$E2FF` cleared (20 rows of 32 and 256 bytes after it); DrawMarks `$E300-$E5FF` set to 1: every character of the play area is drawn on the next DrawMarkedChars and copied once by CopyPlayArea.
> 4. The 135 level bytes go to `$FD23` in 9 rows of 15, each row followed by two zero guards (17 bytes a row): the cell (row r, column c) is at `$FD23` + 17 r + c, and the row above (r = -1) and the guards read as empty cells.
> 5. Falls into RenderGrid (and so DrawMarkedChars): the whole level is drawn into the buffers.
> Called by SetUpLevel (`$8509`) only. The tool `tools/level_maps.py` runs it in SkoolKit's simulator for every slot (docs/img/maps).
> Witness: L1 200 (c1, c1g, cheat, controls, energy, energy-out, hof, kempston, menu, mine, nameedit, overload, practice, L x20, rzx x59).
$8927 BuildLevelAddLoop
$892A BuildLevelGrid ; the grid cleared
$893A ; the character map cleared, every DrawMark 1
$894E ; 9 rows of 15 cells, two guards a row
$8956 BuildLevelRowLoop

@module render ; The renderer: the grid to characters, the buffers, the screen copies, the wipes, the print routines
@about The play area is a character map (CharMap $E000, 20 rows of 32 codes) drawn into a linear pixel buffer (PixelBuffer $E900: a character row is 256 bytes, eight lines of 32) and a colour buffer (ColourBuffer $E600), and copied to the screen only where a mark (DrawMarks $E300, one byte a character, laid out as the screen's character positions) asks: RenderGrid $8960 turns each cell into four characters through CellTable $8200, DrawMarkedChars $8A09 draws the marked ones, CopyPlayArea $8C10 copies the marked ones and counts each mark down.
@about The marks are set by whoever changes a cell: BuildLevel (all, 1), the turning elements (1), the explosions and HighlightCell (2), the beam and the cursor code ($9xxx). The wipes $8C95 / $8CA2 bring a whole buffer onto the screen in a rectangle growing from a random corner; the print routines $8E3A / $8E47 draw text records into the full-screen buffer ($E500 / $E200) or the play buffers.
$8960 c RenderGrid ; Each grid cell to four character codes in the character map; turning elements step on; then DrawMarkedChars
> For the 9 x 15 cells of LevelGrid `$FD23`, CharMapPointer runs from `$E021` (row 1, column 1: the cell (r, c) is the characters (2r+1, 2c+1) to (2r+2, 2c+2)); the cell code's four bytes in CellTable `$8200` + 4 x code are the top-left, top-right, bottom-left and bottom-right character codes.
> A code with bit 7 set is a turning element (RenderGridTurning): the code steps on once a pass, the mirrors `$01-$10` round 16 angles, the blocks `$11-$18` and `$19-$20` round their 8, and the cell's four DrawMarks are set to 1. Other codes with bit 7 (`$A1` up) draw as their low code without turning.
> Writes the map every pass but marks only the turning cells: a cell another routine changes is drawn because that routine marks it.
> Jumps to DrawMarkedChars. From MainLoop (`$8550`) every pass and from BuildLevel (falls in).
> Witness: L1 117459 (c1, c1g, cheat, controls, corner, energy, energy-out, hof, kempston, menu, mine, nameedit, overload, practice, L x20, rzx x59).
$8966 ; the grid, 9 rows of 15
$896B RenderGridRow
$896D RenderGridCell
$8975 RenderGridDraw ; the cell's four codes from CellTable + 4 x code
$897F ; two characters on, then the top row's two and the bottom row's two
$8998 RenderGridNext
$899D ; next row: the map pointer down two rows, the grid past the two guards
$89AE ; draw the marked characters
$89B1 RenderGridTurning ; bit 7: a turning element steps one angle
$89B9 ; mirror $10 back to $01
$89BC RenderGridBlock
$89C3 ; block $18 back to $11
$89C7 RenderGridBlock2
$89CE ; block $20 back to $19
$89D0 RenderGridTurned ; the new code with bit 7 into the grid, its characters into the map
$89F7 ; its four DrawMarks set to 1
$8A09 c DrawMarkedChars ; Draw every marked character into the play buffers, the practice line, the frame round the play area
> For each of the 640 DrawMarks `$E300` with a nonzero mark: the character code at the same place in the character map (`$E000`), its colour `$DF00` + code (CellColours) to ColourBuffer `$E600`, its eight lines `$D700` + 8 x code (CellGraphics) to PixelBuffer `$E900` (row r, column c at `$E900` + 256 r + c, a line every 32 bytes). The marks are left as they are: CopyPlayArea counts them down.
> In practice (PracticeFlag) PrintPlay `$8E47` writes PracticeText on row 19. Then the frame: line 0 and line 159 of the pixel buffer all set, and the left pixel of column 0 and the right pixel of column 31 on lines 1-158.
> From RenderGrid. The practice line `$8A6E` ran 615 times in `practice` (`work/docs/dfA/rec/practice`).
> Witness: L1 117449 (c1, c1g, cheat, controls, corner, energy, energy-out, hof, kempston, menu, mine, nameedit, overload, practice, L x20, rzx x59).
$8A0F DrawMarkedLoop
