$96C3 b CursorVars 16 ; The cursor, the control bits, and the pause's save area
> CursorX `$96C3` (0-14) and CursorY `$96C4` (0-8): the cell under the cursor (0, 0 at the level set-up `$8498`, then the cell in front of the laser, `$8B08`-`$8B2B`; moved by `MoveCursor` `$9910`). ControlBits `$96C5`: this pass's controls from `ReadControls` `$9869` (bit 0 left, 1 right, 2 down, 3 up, 4 fire). CursorMode `$96C6`: 0, or 7 while fire is held (cleared by `ReadKeys` `$97F0` each pass, set by `$995E` and `CursorFire` `$9A57`), which `DrawCursor` `$99C6` shows as a white square instead of inverted colours.
> PauseGame `$973A` keeps here what the INTERMISSION banner overwrites: the COMPUTER line's 14 bytes `$A104`-`$A111` (`$96C7`), the energy tick `$A506` (`$96D5`) and the sound flags `$A8A6` (`$96D6`), and five pixel rows of 16 bytes of the screen at `$50E0` (`$96DB`). `$96D7`-`$96DA` are never used.
