$A02A ; GREAT (row 10)
$A032 ; GOOD (row 11)
$A03A ; SO-SO (row 12)
$A042 ; BAD (row 13)
$A04A ; AWFUL (row 14)
$A052 ; the end of the list

@module menu ; Title, options panel, demo, practice, the hall of fame display
$A053 b OptionsLayout 2 ; The options screen's layout: 87 runs (count, value) giving 24 x 32 cells, $FF
> Read by `$9ED8` (at `$9EDB`): each pair writes `count` copies of `value` to `$E200` on, `$FF` ends; the 87 runs fill exactly 768 cells (24 rows of 32). Values: `$00` empty, `$3B` and `$38` the attributes of the title box (rows 1-2, magenta on white) and of the two panels (rows 5-17: the OPTIONS and HALL OF FAME boxes; rows 20-23: the scroller's box), `$02` a shadow cell: `$9ED8` draws the checker pattern `$9F41` (`$AA55...`) into the pixel buffer `$E500` wherever a cell is `$02`, the drop shadow along the right and bottom edge of each box.
> Decoded (`.` `$00`, `b` `$3B`, `w` `$38`, `#` `$02`): rows 1-2 cols 7-23 `b`, its shadow on row 3; rows 5-17 two boxes cols 0-13 and 17-30 `w`, shadows in col 14 / 31 and row 18; rows 20-22 cols 4-26 `w`, shadow col 27 and row 23.
> Evidence: read 12 times (every draw of the options screen: `c1g`, `menu`, `controls`, `kempston`, `mine`, `overload`, `gameover`, `rzx-344752`).
@res tables/options-layout.bin
$A101 ; the end mark
$A102 b UnusedA102 ; One byte $FF that no recording reads or writes
> No instruction in the image addresses it (searched in `game.skool`); probably a spare end mark of the layout above.

@module panel ; The HUD panel and the COMPUTER line: the message variables and texts
@about The COMPUTER line (row 23, columns 1-15) is driven by the interrupt (InterruptHandler $A32A): the game only writes the address of a message to MessageText $A10E, and a message number to MessageNumber $A104 (most writers only when the message is more urgent than the one shown). A message that starts with $FE is static (14 characters, blinking); any other scrolls in from the right a pixel a frame, its $FF followed by the address where it goes on (a loop, or BlankMessage $A199, which ends it). The same line in the menu (row 21, columns 5-25, MenuScroller $A103 set) scrolls the credits and the name-entry prompt, where a byte $FE is a pause counted down in the text itself.
$A103 b MenuScroller ; $FF: the interrupt runs the menu's scroller (row 21) and counts nothing; 0: the game's COMPUTER line
> Set by the menu set-up `$9BC0` (at `$9BC7`), cleared by OptionsMenu `$A757` when a game starts (`$A804`). While set, InterruptHandler `$A32A` jumps to MenuScrollerTick `$A459` and neither EnergyTick `$A506` nor FrameCounter `$837F` is counted. Evidence: read by every interrupt (381 862 in all recordings), written 19 times.
$A104 b MessageNumber ; The number of the message shown: 0 none ... $18 CONTACT!; most writers replace only a lower one
> GREMLINS, ENERGY LOW, CRITICAL and BOOM compare first (`CP n` / `JR NC`) and write only when the current number is lower. CHARGING LASER (a level start), MINE ALERT, GAME ABORTED, ENERGY DRAINED and CONTACT! write with no test; OVERLOAD writes when the number is below `$12` or is MINE ALERT's `$13` (`$A6B3`); CoolOverload `$A6FC` blanks OVERLOAD and MINE ALERT. The numbers: 1 CHARGING LASER / DEMO (ResetBars `$A55E`), 4 BEWARE OF THE GREMLINS (`$AC21`), `$0A` ENERGY LOW (`$A665`), `$0C` ENERGY LEVEL CRITICAL (`$A62F`), `$12` OVERLOAD (`$A6BD`), `$13` MINE ALERT (`$A68B`), `$14` GAME / DEMO ABORTED (`$9816`), `$16` BOOM BOOM BOOM (`$8677`), `$17` ENERGY DRAINED (`$A671`), `$18` CONTACT! (`$87DA`, the beam has reached the receiver). 0 again when a scrolling message runs back into BlankMessage (`$A3F0`) or the overload stops (`$A708`).
> The pause `$973F` saves the 14 bytes MessageNumber to MessagePointer (`$A104-$A111`) to `$96C7` and puts them back (`$97DD`). Evidence: `energy` (`tools/ttd_watch.py`): 1 at frame 500, `$0A` at 5000, `$0C` at 5750, `$17` at 6450.
$A105 b MessageGlyph 8 ; The character being scrolled in: its 8 font bytes; rows 2-6 ($A107-$A10B) are shifted out a bit a frame
> Filled by `LDIR` from the font (`$D200 + 8 x (c - 32)`) at `$A405` / `$A4E2`; each scroll step rotates rows 2-6 left (`RLA`) and the carry goes into the line's rightmost byte. Rows 0, 1 and 7 are copied but never shifted (the line shows 5 pixel rows).
$A10D b MessageState ; The scroller's state: 0-7 the pixel within a scrolling character; $E6-$FF a static message's blink phase
> Scrolling: counts 0 to 8; at 8 the next character is loaded (`$A3D3`, `$A490`). Static: `$E6-$EF` the line blank, `$F0` the text drawn, `$F1-$FE` shown, `$FF` the line cleared and back to `$E6` (`$A36E`): 15 frames on, 10 off.
$A10E w MessageText ; The next message: the game writes its address here; the interrupt takes it and clears the high byte
> A message is pending while the high byte (`$A10F`) is not 0 (every message lies at `$A1xx-$A2xx`). The interrupt copies the word to MessagePointer and writes 0 to `$A10F` (`$A35B`, `$A45F`). Writers: SetupInterrupts (BlankMessage), `$8435`, ResetBars, `$A5F7`, DrainEnergy, UpdateOverload, GremlinAppear, `$867D`, `$87E0`, `$97B4`, `$9822`, `$9BF6`, `$9CB4`, OptionsMenu.
$A110 w MessagePointer ; The text being shown: the next character of a scrolling message, or the $FE of a static one

$A112 t DemoMessage ; Static: ",,,, DEMO ,,,," (MessageNumber 1, ResetBars on demo level 0)
> 14 characters after the `$FE` static mark; `,` is a small ring in the font (`$D260`), `.` a small diamond. Evidence: read in `menu` (the demo).
@res texts/messages.bin
$A121 t ChargingMessage ; Static: "CHARGING LASER" (MessageNumber 1, ResetBars)
> Shown at each level start while the energy bar fills. Evidence: `energy` frame 500; every recording that started a level.
@res texts/messages.bin
$A130 t OverloadMessage ; Static: " . OVERLOAD . " (MessageNumber $12, the beam back in the laser)
> Evidence: `overload`; read in `mine` and 54 RZX segments.
@res texts/messages.bin
$A13F t MineAlertMessage ; Static: ". MINE ALERT ." (MessageNumber $13, the beam on a mine)
> Evidence: `mine`; 46 RZX segments.
@res texts/messages.bin
$A14E t DrainedMessage ; Static: "ENERGY DRAINED" (MessageNumber $17, EnergyDrained $A66F)
> Evidence: `energy` (twice), `rzx-053912`, `rzx-227686`.
@res texts/messages.bin
$A15D t BoomMessage ; Static: "BOOM BOOM BOOM" (MessageNumber $16, a life lost: $867A)
> Evidence: `mine`, `overload`, `gameover` and the RZX segments that lost a life.
@res texts/messages.bin
$A16C t ContactMessage ; Static: "   CONTACT!   " (MessageNumber $18, the beam reached the receiver: $87DD)
> Shown by `$87D4` when LevelDone `$8ED2` is set, the level complete. Evidence: read in all 60 RZX segments (each reaches the end of a level in the RZX's own run).
@res texts/messages.bin
$A17B t GameAbortedMessage ; Static: " GAME ABORTED " (MessageNumber $14, U + G: $9811)
> Evidence: `controls`, `kempston`, `menu`.
@res texts/messages.bin
