> The 14 characters end at `$A198`; BlankMessage follows.
@res texts/messages.bin
$A199 t BlankMessage ; Scrolling: two spaces, then back to itself: the line runs empty; reaching it ends a message (MessageNumber 0)
> The "no message" message: SetupInterrupts, `$8435`, the end of charging (`$A602`), the overload stopping (`$A70B`), `$9BF3`. The scroller compares every `$FF` jump with this address (`$A3E7`) and clears MessageNumber when it is taken.
@res texts/messages.bin
$A19B ; $FF, then the address where the text goes on
$A19C w BlankMessageLoop ; BlankMessage again
@res texts/messages.bin
