$D1C0 b SpareD1C0 16 ; 64 bytes of 0 after the last level slot, below the font's first character
> No instruction addresses `$D1C0-$D1FF` and no recording reads or writes it. The printers address the font as `$D200` + 8 x (code - 32), so a notional base `$D100` would put characters 24-31 here; nothing prints a code below 32.
@res leftovers/spare-d1c0.bin

@module render
$D200 b Font 8 ; The text font: 96 characters 32-127, 8 bytes each (glyph = $D200 + 8 x (code - 32))
> Read by the printers PrintFull `$8E3A` / PrintPlay `$8E47` (`$8E87`, `LD BC,$D200`), the COMPUTER line and the menu line (`$A3B0`, `$A401`, `$A4DE`: `$D202` / `$D200`, glyph rows 2-6 scrolled), the score (`$9B1D`), the pause (`$9787`), and as the blank space glyph `$D200` (`$9CF9`, `$9D3B`, `$9DFA`, `$A82C`).
> Characters 32-90: the text (`,` a small ring, `.` a small diamond, `@` the copyright sign, `[`-`_` unused); characters `$61-$7A` with `(` and `)` are the 2 x 15 pieces of the DEFLEKTOR logo of the options screen (OptionsText `$9F59`: "(abcdefghijklm(" over ")nopqrstuvwxyz)"); `$7B-$7F` are blank. Characters no recording printed: 34-39, 42, 43, 47, 58-63, 81, 90-96, 123-127 (the COMPUTER and menu lines read only rows 2-6 of a glyph). Editable form: graphics/font.png.
$D200 ; characters 32-47 (space, punctuation)
$D280 ; characters 48-63 (the digits, then : ; and ?)
$D300 ; characters 64-79 (@ the copyright sign, A-O)
$D380 ; characters 80-95 (P-Z)
$D400 ; characters 96-111 (the logo's top row a-m)
$D480 ; characters 112-127 (the logo's bottom row n-z; 123-127 blank)
@res graphics/font.bin

@module beam
$D500 b BeamGlyphs 8 ; The beam's 39 glyphs (8 bytes each): $D500 + 8 x the glyph number of BeamGlyphBytes
> ORed into the pixel buffer `$E900` by BeamPlotGlyph (`$92C3`), BeamCornerChar (`$9483`) and BeamOutPlot (`$954A`), one character a glyph, with the colour `$43`. Glyph numbers come only from BeamGlyphBytes `$8000`, whose largest is 38: so the glyphs end at `$D637`. Glyphs 28 and 36 were drawn by no recording. Editable form: graphics/beam-glyphs.png.
@res graphics/beam-glyphs.bin
$D638 b SpareBeamGlyphs 8 ; 25 glyph slots past the last glyph BeamGlyphBytes names: 14 dotted beam drawings, then zeros
> No glyph byte of BeamGlyphBytes reaches glyphs 39-63 (`$D638-$D6FF`), and no recording reads them. Glyphs 39-52 hold beam pieces drawn as dotted lines (slopes and diagonals); 53-63 are zeros. A third glyph set the tables do not use: leftovers/beam-glyphs-spare.png.
@res leftovers/beam-glyphs-spare.bin

@module render
$D700 b CellGraphics 8 ; The 212 characters of the cell elements, 8 bytes each, characters $00-$D3 (CellTable's codes)
> DrawMarkedChars `$8A09` (`$8A2A`) draws a marked character from `$D700` + 8 x code, its colour from CellColours `$DF00` + code (`$8A1C`, `LD H,$DF`). Character 0 is the empty background (four dots); the beam's wipes (`$937C`, `$93C7`, `$95FA`, `$9645`) copy it over a glyph to erase it.
> Characters: `$01-$30` the mirrors' art, `$31-$50` the cyan polarisers', `$51-$70` the yellow ones', `$71` the absorbing wall quarter, `$72` the reflecting one, `$73` unused (zeros), `$74-$77` the cell, `$78-$7B` the mine, `$7C-$7F` the prism, `$80-$8F` the cyan lasers (codes `$43-$46`, unused), `$90-$9F` the lasers, `$A0-$AF` the receivers, `$B0-$BF` the four fibre-optic pictures, `$C0-$D3` the explosion's five frames. CellTable names no character above `$D3`. Editable form: graphics/cells.png, with CellColours.
$D700 ; $00 the empty background
$D708 ; $01-$30 the mirrors
$D888 ; $31-$50 the cyan polarisers
$D988 ; $51-$70 the yellow polarisers
$DA88 ; $71 absorbing wall, $72 reflecting wall, $73 unused
$DAA0 ; $74-$77 cell, $78-$7B mine, $7C-$7F prism
$DB00 ; $80-$8F the cyan lasers (unused)
$DB80 ; $90-$9F the lasers (east, south, west, north)
$DC00 ; $A0-$AF the receivers
$DC80 ; $B0-$BF the fibre-optic ends
$DD00 ; $C0-$D3 the explosion's frames
@res graphics/cell-graphics.bin
$DDA0 b SpareCellGraphics 32 ; 352 bytes of 0: the graphics of characters $D4-$FF, which no cell code names
> CellTable's largest character is `$D3`, so `$D700` + 8 x `$D4` onwards (`$DDA0-$DEFF`) is never drawn; no recording reads it.
@res leftovers/cell-graphics-spare.bin
$DF00 b CellColours 16 ; The attribute of each character $00-$D3 of CellGraphics
> Read by DrawMarkedChars (`$8A1C`): `$43` (bright magenta on black) the background, the cell and the mine; `$04` the mirrors (green); `$0D` the cyan polarisers; `$16` the yellow ones and the reflecting wall quarter; `$42` the absorbing wall quarter; `$17` the prism; `$05` the cyan lasers; `$07` the lasers and receivers; `$38-$3B` the four fibre-optic pictures (black on white, blue, red, magenta); `$47`, `$46`, `$06`, `$42` the explosion's frames. Not read: `$DF73` (character `$73`, `$07`) and `$DF80-$DF8F` (the cyan lasers). Editable form: graphics/cells.png.
$DF00 ; $00-$0F
$DF70 ; $70-$7F
$DFC0 ; $C0-$D3 the explosion
@res graphics/cell-colours.bin
$DFD4 b SpareCellColours 16 ; 44 bytes of 0: the colours of characters $D4-$FF, never read
> As SpareCellGraphics: no character above `$D3` is drawn; no recording reads `$DFD4-$DFFF`.
@res leftovers/cell-colours-spare.bin
